{"title":"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there are infinitely many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557bd457147e3f9d72ec7454eca375f34c4ccf2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> has a prime divisor greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7afda4da9915ce8287d53374fb10a8695c2551c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n + \\sqrt {2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Solution 1</b>\n</p><p>The main idea is to take a gaussian prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615e780fda439b2829922a704a60b31c5ed77191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and multiply it by a \"twice as small\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69b5d9cfbac40e0d795398b0648b92ed41ca48ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+di$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a862acd63d0a565db8f2a6ca87c7d7d8784924e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />. The rest is just making up the little details.\n</p><p>For each <i>sufficiently large</i> prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e72c7016c6369f44ebe1c8cef90078a2a8dd3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, we shall find a corresponding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f55a7827b23d850bed0d0c3bf0880b27ffcca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28f59adb81a543f8c612f3106b75a660a7bfed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;2n+\\sqrt{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"23\" />. Since there exist infinitely many such primes and, for each of them, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec5a35d306724df9f05e12fe757ebb9512152ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge \\sqrt{p-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"22\" />, we will have found infinitely many <i>distinct</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the hypothesis.\n</p><p>Take a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e72c7016c6369f44ebe1c8cef90078a2a8dd3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and consider its \"sum-of-two squares\" representation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8338a297ff57485820927efca3fe94850c375f1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />, which we know to exist for all such primes. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18c60d7d33b7407a1b630a8f55755407bb16ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ne b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, assume without loss of generality that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc685c058a3923bc44dc7a591ea65066c69dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd2d550e9cf88b2ee99204c6b3f165e03b0a459d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=b$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is what we are looking for, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5cb3dc0d25f21617fe85448e2c5846f0128ad31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=n^2+1 &gt; 2n+\\sqrt{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" /> as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />) is large enough. Assume from now on that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd78bcb8d40ee2dc69cf5e7ca921a4e80b7b3b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are (obviously) co-prime, there must exist integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aad253c3cfc9a53c8d158f70b1a1a8d5d355dcb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ad+bc=1. \\quad(1)\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />\nIn fact, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are such numbers, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/16911280417bd0737b860d0d519b79ecb9aaa0f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\pm ma$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c638dc19b4755a926ef3cf539c6eb41f485d1698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\mp mb$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> work as well for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, so we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b2032bee50a74fa9ea766e970c29bdc0663fb8c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\in \\left[-\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{a}{2}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/5134442637afc2757f86906df4a514de8696407c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=|ac-bd|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> and let's see why this is a good choice. For starters, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f969079dd6a918de04f8b654bc4204dc66c511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2+b^2)(c^2+d^2)=n^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba82583dd5d8626a5a2cd8d8a735203bea6c6bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\pm\\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"33\" />, from (1) we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. This implies, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3ec0e5df637490d34cafc562fcc2e55fa75fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=-\\frac{b-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f1048915483ed41aeef0f0d53588d71fd16f044c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{b(b-1)}{2}-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e67aa1428b67da7e9f2b223efedd01172a0e671b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(b-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = 1/4 + 2(n+2) &gt; 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"259\" height=\"46\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d30ec27a139c741c84c68a7b90190756a9896b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; \\sqrt{2n}+\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b70660eb9a8fea201a0b5482afef058665f2aa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=b^2+2^2 &gt; 2n+\\sqrt{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" /> and the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba82583dd5d8626a5a2cd8d8a735203bea6c6bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\pm\\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"33\" /> is cleared.\n</p><p>We can safely assume now that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd2cae8f90ce6da8d91a11c1ccf23ff45df0f0c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|c| \\le \\frac{a-1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd78bcb8d40ee2dc69cf5e7ca921a4e80b7b3b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94ebd084e8b6801c5791566f5bb434fb1b76abc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/92647205e550eb2bd7bb9f6b2a503a1bb05b1184.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|d| = \\left|\\frac{1-bc}{a}\\right| \\le \\frac{b(a-1)+2}{2a} &lt; \\frac{ba}{2a} = \\frac{b}{2},\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"43\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a2b9e09cf209c0aac55969d27ff33a6f644da1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|d| \\le \\frac{b-1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab277f1d80473bbf2c493e8bc3d4c4dfec79493f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2+1 = (a^2+b^2)(c^2+d^2) \\le p\\left( \\frac{(a-1)^2}{4}+\\frac{(b-1)^2}{4} \\right). \\quad (2)\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"43\" /> \n</p><p>Before we proceed, we would like to show first that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edad860b294fbc1f3f2b70026aeeb6e646e366ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b-1 &gt; \\sqrt{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. Observe that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c287df1ede212ae34cd49667750db87c2380992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\sqrt{p-x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"22\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f605cc4eea4b18a14fbfac2dfccf8c8cb1377fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in(2,\\sqrt{p-4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"22\" /> reaches its minima on the ends, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa0dd1b71a19b648d715d384f9874911a1df3c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> is minimized for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, where it equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/533e2ea39262416b1acf4f732e97a92022c0803d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+\\sqrt{p-2^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"22\" />. So we want to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a7534e4bc9348a7b8f801723e0c25e70eba73dd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2+\\sqrt{p-4} &gt; \\sqrt{p} + 1,\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"22\" />\nwhich is not hard to show for <i>large enough</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Now armed with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1cd77a96350974dfd9e000789b8914eb69e8d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b-1&gt;\\sqrt{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> and (2), we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca811baceadd330a22e7e6e9ed57cdb88bf9cf4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4(n^2+1)\\le p( a^2+b^2 - 2(a+b-1) )&lt; p( p-2\\sqrt{p} )&lt; u^2(u-1)^2,\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"20\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e3106a171c53ff5667c46dc2d3394538cbc2f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=\\sqrt{p}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Finally, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d54577c715eec7a70304a2149a3cfded68df376f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u^2(u-1)^2 &gt; 4n^2+4 &gt; 4n^2\\Rightarrow u(u-1) &gt; 2n \\Rightarrow  (u-\\frac{1}{2})^2 &gt; 2n+\\frac{1}{4} &gt; 2n \\Rightarrow u &gt; \\sqrt{2n} + \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow  p = u^2 &gt; 2n + \\sqrt{2n}.\\]\" width=\"835\" height=\"37\" />\nThe proof is complete.\n</p><p><b>Solution 2</b>\n</p><p>We begin with a lemma.\n</p><p>Lemma: For every prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9f0f2a5ebd30ad7a70a041deb220fe03bb11fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\mod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12ffdfc9f88d12b5c8330407caae501c50645aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\le \\dfrac{p - \\sqrt{p-4}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3a9d5a47974d0bcfb0dc1cf2420289217d5695e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\mid n^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Proof:\nWe know that there must be a solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38b64759322b54ff940d88dbf393812e407c9fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+1 \\equiv 0 \\mod{p}\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" />\nwith <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4662ee3c0aebda4f794ff3bea0c427555ab088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le x \\le p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.  However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a solution then so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf04a3839bdda520f4a0e069ce6fe6dd508de57a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" />, so there must be a solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd9d89336c379dc4a230981a4ae26a152559f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> denote this solution and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cfa02e41aa4aa0c33d8b55ef1adce94aed005c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{p-k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" />.  Then, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe523fad6b62877b4b7e52b7e62cb40a4ac3343.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\dfrac{p-k}{2}\\right)^2 \\equiv -1 \\mod{p}\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/589814b9cd2b8bf375fefcdf26798d2eeef4c405.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2 \\equiv -4 \\mod{p}.\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca20124205ccc001262b72ce8c5826df2e14d391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 \\ge p-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />, so we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad7890f6cf1fb55ad3473d4a20bf760eccbb1ce1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\le \\dfrac{p - \\sqrt{p-4}}{2},\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"39\" />\nas desired.  The lemma is proven.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Suppose for sake of contradiction that there are only finitely many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e46503c75923193299de31772ba81145aa45602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1,n_2,\\dots,n_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> that work.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9f0f2a5ebd30ad7a70a041deb220fe03bb11fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\mod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> be a prime with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284ed6cae10d30745c885b41f602eba010474f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad0b4b91f7603f623ef60e47f991fd05b6501df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> (the existence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is guaranteed by the existence of infinitely many primes of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e72c7016c6369f44ebe1c8cef90078a2a8dd3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />).  Then, we know that there exists an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdf878abaabd3fc9f980317c1efa39a50ca5a330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\le \\dfrac{p - \\sqrt{p-4}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/628568f19b221fe2569274204082ff68dc3eb807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p | N^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" /> (this last condition shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is not among <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e46503c75923193299de31772ba81145aa45602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1,n_2,\\dots,n_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" />.  We want to show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1feef7d9919c3584a9415c22f4f20f9eb6144b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p &gt; 2N + \\sqrt{2N}\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e8608f9946bcc2df300c974e0f7c151e240252.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p - 2N &gt; \\sqrt{2N}.\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />\nBut, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b338c4ef8f12752075ed22dcf89727c2ae606540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-2N \\ge \\sqrt{p-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" />, so it suffices to show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/8442b3a389eadaf90ceb3092185341354d0aa9db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p-4 &gt; 2N\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/27240c3e5826d5270e3482e9f1da0e8a875c67b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p - 2N &gt; 4.\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\nOnce again, it suffices to show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324622c77758ea270f45c50ac86eb2a8958c6b88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{p-4} &gt; 4,\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"22\" />\nwhich follows from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284ed6cae10d30745c885b41f602eba010474f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies the required condition and it follows that there exist infinitely many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy the given condition, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO\" title=\"2008 IMO\">2008 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017215542\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 560/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19100/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.786      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.786      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7239:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017215542 and revision id 204530. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}